em>Romeo and Juliet</em>&nbsp;is still relevant for young people today because</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>it illustrates how easily conflict can start.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>it deals with problems that families experience.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>it teaches them about relationships.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span>The students found watching&nbsp;<em>Romeo and Juliet</em>&nbsp;in another language</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>frustrating.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>demanding.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>moving.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span>Why do the students think Shakespeare’s plays have such international appeal?</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>The stories are exciting.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>There are recognisable characters.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>They can be interpreted in many ways.</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":3}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-17-academic-listening-2-audio-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-c17-t2-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/13587-cambridge-ielts-17-academic-listening-2-audio-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c17-t2-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p><em>Complete the notes below.</em></p><p><em>Write&nbsp;<strong>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER</strong>&nbsp;for each answer.</em></p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong><strong>The impact of digital technology on the Icelandic language</strong></strong></p><p><strong>The Icelandic language</strong></p><ul><li>has approximately <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;speakers</li><li>has a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;that is still growing</li><li>has not changed a lot over the last thousand years</li><li>has its own words for computer-based concepts, such as web browser and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul><p><strong>Young speakers</strong></p><ul><li>are big users of digital technology, such as <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>are becoming <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;very quickly</li><li>are having discussions using only English while they are in the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;at school</li><li>are better able to identify the content of a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;in English than Icelandic</li></ul><p><strong>Technology and internet companies</strong></p><ul><li>write very little in Icelandic because of the small number of speakers and because of how complicated its <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;is</li></ul><p><strong>The Icelandic government</strong></p><ul><li>has set up a fund to support the production of more digital content in the language</li><li>believes that Icelandic has a secure future</li><li>is worried that young Icelanders may lose their <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;as Icelanders</li><li>is worried about the consequences of children not being <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c17-t2-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;in either Icelandic or English</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-17-academic-listening-2-audio-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c17-t2-l-q1","part_id":"en-c17-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c17-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"collecting","correct_answer_variants":["collecting"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_13541_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-c17-t2-l-q2","part_id":"en-c17-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c17-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"records","correct_answer_variants":["records"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_13541_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-c17-t2-l-q3","part_id":"en-c17-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c17-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"West","correct_answer_variants":["West"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[3],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_13541_3","order_index":3,"points":1},{"id":"en-c17-t2-l-q4","